{
  "cargo_semantics": [
    "N rustc only counts unused extern error severity as a compiler error in loud mode. unused-externs-silent therefore prevents deriving arbitrary Cargo success from rustc rc0 alone.",
    "The captured force-warn flag is sticky and fixes the native record level here. Accepting a deny/forbid record under that fixed command would conceal a contract change.",
    "Reviewed Cargo source separately aggregates unused dependencies and applies manifest-level Cargo lints after child completion; deny/forbid can contribute an overall Cargo failure even when an individual rustc exited zero.",
    "A nonempty force-warn list remains legitimate frontend output to preserve and compare; it is not automatically an end-to-end Cargo success result."
  ],
  "cargo_source": {
